KFLOPPY-DOS PS-100/200 Floppy Disk Drive Emulator supplimental information

This file contains supplemetal information not given in the manual.

New command option switch

The KFLOPPY interactive menus only update the screen during vertical retrace
if a Color Graphics Adapter (CGA) video card is being used.  This is to 
prevent the "snow" or "green lightning" that is present on the original
IBM PC.  On the old 8088 PCs, this makes the menus run slow and there is a
delay from when a key is pressed and an action is displayed.  If your PC
has a CGA card but is not subject to snow, you can disable this feature.
By using the "/s" switch on the command line, you can speed up the menus:

	C:\> KFLOPPY /s

This disables snow suppression.  If you perform a "Save settings" from the
"Setup" menu, the command "Snow On" will be put in the initialization file.

Operational Limitations

The mouse cursor disappears and the mouse is disabled while the "Emulate"
panel is displayed.  You must use the keyboard to stop emulation.  Once the
"Emulate" panel is removed, mouse operation is re-enabled.

